{"q":"209","t":"Minimum Size Subarray Sum","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an array of positive integers <code>nums</code> and a positive integer <code>target</code>, return <em>the <strong>minimal length</strong> of a </em><span data-keyword=\"subarray-nonempty\"><em>subarray</em></span><em> whose sum is greater than or equal to</em> <code>target</code>. If there is no such subarray, return <code>0</code> instead.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> target = 7, nums = [2,3,1,2,4,3]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The subarray [4,3] has the minimal length under the problem constraint.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> target = 4, nums = [1,4,4]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> target = 11, nums = [1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= target &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow up:</strong> If you have figured out the <code>O(n)</code> solution, try coding another solution of which the time complexity is <code>O(n log(n))</code>.","h":[],"m":"{\n  \"name\": \"minSubArrayLen\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"target\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"return\": {\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\n  }\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Binary Search","slug":"binary-search"},{"name":"Sliding Window","slug":"sliding-window"},{"name":"Prefix Sum","slug":"prefix-sum"}],"s":[{"t":"Minimum Window Substring","s":"minimum-window-substring","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Size Subarray Sum Equals k","s":"maximum-size-subarray-sum-equals-k","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Length of Repeated Subarray","s":"maximum-length-of-repeated-subarray","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Operations to Reduce X to Zero","s":"minimum-operations-to-reduce-x-to-zero","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"K Radius Subarray Averages","s":"k-radius-subarray-averages","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Product After K Increments","s":"maximum-product-after-k-increments","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Shortest Subarray With OR at Least K I","s":"shortest-subarray-with-or-at-least-k-i","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Positive Sum Subarray ","s":"minimum-positive-sum-subarray","d":"Easy","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Meta","facebook"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["DoorDash","doordash"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Nvidia","nvidia"],["Apple","apple"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",9],["Meta","facebook",8],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",4],["Microsoft","microsoft",3],["Amazon","amazon",3]],"b":[],"m":[["BCG","bcg",8],["DoorDash","doordash",7],["TikTok","tiktok",6],["Oracle","oracle",3],["tcs","tcs",2],["Apple","apple",2],["Goldman Sachs","goldman-sachs",2],["DE Shaw","de-shaw",2],["Nvidia","nvidia",2],["Yandex","yandex",2]]}}